<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
  <!--
    Nothing of its own, on purpose.

    No permission: the contact picker is ACTION_PICK, which hands back one row
    the app may read once and needs no READ_CONTACTS, and ACCESS_COARSE_LOCATION
    belongs to the app's own list (app.config.ts), where it can be seen beside
    the blocked ones.

    HealthRationaleActivity is in this module's Kotlin but is NOT declared here:
    plugin/withTulmiPerms.js writes the activity and its VIEW_PERMISSION_USAGE
    alias into the app's manifest only when the Android health build switch is
    on. A build without Health Connect must have no health entry at all.
  -->
</manifest>
